Step 1: A ∪ B (union) contains all elements from both sets.
A ∪ B = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}

Step 2: A ∩ B (intersection) contains only common elements.
A ∩ B = {4, 5}

Final Answer: A ∪ B = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}, A ∩ B = {4, 5}

Step 1: A' (complement of A) contains all elements of universal set U that are NOT in A.
Step 2: Elements in U but not in A are: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10

Final Answer: A' = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10}

Step 1: Factors of 12 are numbers that divide 12 evenly.
Factors: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12
So A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12}

Step 2: Multiples of 2 that are ≤ 12 are: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12
So B = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12}

Final Answer: A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12}, B = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12}

Step 1: Power set P(A) contains all possible subsets of A.
Step 2: Subsets of {1, 2}:
- ∅ (empty set)
- {1}
- {2}
- {1, 2}

Step 3: A set with n elements has 2ⁿ subsets. Here n = 2, so 2² = 4 subsets.

Final Answer: P(A) = {∅, {1}, {2}, {1, 2}}
